@startuml
title ASUC-04c - Adapt to energy conditions: relocate flexible workloads (UC4)
autonumber "<b>00"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam dpi 140
skinparam maxMessageSize 170
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #555555
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFF4F4
  ParticipantBorderColor #B52330
  ActorBackgroundColor #EEEEEE
  ActorBorderColor #202025
  GroupBorderColor #B52330
}
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FAF5F5
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B52330

actor "Time\nTrigger" as TT
participant "Event\nBus" as EB
participant "Placement\nController" as PC
participant "Policy\nEngine" as POL
participant "Kubernetes\nAPI" as K8S <<external>>
database "Data\nStore" as DB
participant "Telemetry" as TEL

== Trigger ==
EB -> PC : modeChanged(from, to, reason)
TT -> PC : reconcile() every 5 minutes (repairs a lost event)

== Decide the target pool ==
PC -> POL : current()
POL --> PC : mode, placement target
PC -> PC : target pool := the placement target stored with the mode\n(eco for AMBER, RED or renewable available; standard otherwise)
PC -> K8S : listNodes(pool labels, readiness)
K8S --> PC : nodes with pool label, ready state and taints
PC -> PC : safety checks: both pools have a ready node,\nthe last placement change is older than the dwell time (15 min),\nthe change would not leave zero schedulable nodes
alt a check fails or the target equals the current placement
  PC -> DB : record the decision as SKIPPED (reason)
  PC -> TEL : placementSkipped(reason)
else placement changes
  == Act ==
  PC -> K8S : taint the non-target pool energy-role=blocked (NoExecute);\nremove the taint from the target pool
  K8S --> PC : taints applied
  K8S -> K8S : evict pods that do not tolerate the taint\n(forecast Jobs, local model runtime) and reschedule them on the target pool
  note right of K8S
    Request-path pods, the database, the event bus and monitoring
    carry a toleration and never move. Evicted Jobs are idempotent
    and leased, so they are retried before their deadline.
  end note
  PC -> DB : record the decision (mode, target pool, reason, outcome APPLIED)
  PC -> TEL : placementChanged(from pool, to pool, mode)
end

note over PC, TEL
  Taints are touched only when the decision changes, otherwise every loop would evict pods.
  The simulated pools stand for a low-carbon or low-price node group; the speed difference
  between the pools is measured, not assumed (carbon-adaptation.md).
end note
@enduml
